lines.english:
“Ah… ahaha… ha…”

Setsuna turned the shower on full and let water cold enough to freeze body and soul pound over her. Inside its roar, she at last released everything she had held down.

Only self-loathing circled through her mind:

for ruining her own happiness;

for learning to lie so easily even to her family;

for what the lie had been about;

for becoming someone who could protect her identity only by hurting herself.

“Ahaha… ahahahaha…”

Setsuna had reverted to the girl she had been a year before:

always in the middle of the crowd and always alone—the old ‘Ogiso.’
